`ifndef HISI_IO_CONFIG_CV300_RDL
`define HISI_IO_CONFIG_CV300_RDL

regfile eHISI_IO_CONFIG_CV300 {
    name = "IO configuration: pin multiplexing (0x0..0x104) and pad control (0x800..0x92F), Hi3516C V300 / Hi3516E V100";
    desc = "
    Window 0x12040000 (mux, 66 registers, one per pin, function field [2:0]) and 0x12040800 (pad control, 76 registers). The data sheet gives only the memory-map rows for these windows and no register table (Table 1-1): this file is built from VENDOR DEVICE TREE data, not from the data sheet.
    PROVENANCE. Source: OpenIPC linux-openipc-upstream arch/arm/boot/dts/hisilicon/hi3516cv300.dtsi (pinctrl-single node: reg 0x12040000 size 0x108, function-mask 7, register-width 32; pinconf-single node: reg 0x12040800 size 0x130) and hi3516cv300-demb.dts (HiSilicon demo board pin groups). PROVEN (vendor dts, the vendor kernel programs exactly this): the window sizes, the 3-bit function field, and every (register offset, function value, signal) triple listed in the enums below. The dts gpio-range says pins 0-53 and 61-65 are GPIO at function 0 and pins 55-60 are GPIO at function 1 (pin 54 has no GPIO); the pin index of a register is offset/4 (INFERRED from the range arithmetic). The dts lists only the functions the demo board uses, so a function value that is missing in an enum is UNKNOWN, not reserved. Pad names are not given by any source except the signal comments of the dts (taken verbatim as enum names); register names are muxctrl_regN with N = offset/4 (GUESS, the vendor does not name them). Not hardware verified.
    Pad control registers (0x800 + offset of the pin, 76 registers): the dts writes drive-strength groups with mask 0xFF and the values 0x00, 0x10, 0x20, 0x30, 0x31, 0x40, 0x50, 0x70 (PROVEN as written values); a 3-bit drive-strength code in bits [6:4] is INFERRED from those values and bit 0 (set in 0x31 once) is a GUESS; the other bits are not described.
    ";

